ipvolt's commitment
-------------------
ipvolt, a proxy provider, started and maintains scrapescope. We commit that:

1. scrapescope stays free and MIT-licensed. There is no paid tier, licence key,
   usage limit or feature held back for ipvolt customers, and we will not
   relicense existing or future releases under more restrictive terms.
2. scrapescope works with any proxy provider, or with no provider at all
   (direct "sizing" mode). It has no ipvolt default upstream, rate or account,
   and it never favours ipvolt in what it measures or recommends.
3. scrapescope never contacts ipvolt. It has no telemetry, analytics, crash
   reporting or update checks. It makes network connections only on behalf of
   the job you run through it, the page you ask `scrapescope find` to load, and
   the single replay request you ask for with `--verify`.

If a release ever breaks one of these commitments, treat it as a bug and report
it as described in SECURITY.md.

Third-party material
--------------------
Some challenge-page detection signals in src/scrapescope/catalog/challenges.json
are adapted from is-antibot (https://github.com/microlinkhq/is-antibot), used
under the MIT License. They are used only to classify a response as a
challenge or block page, never to get past one. Each signal in
challenges.json lists its own sources.

Adapted from is-antibot: the body marker _cf_chl_opt and the cf_clearance
cookie (Cloudflare); gokuProps and the aws-waf-token cookie (AWS WAF);
x-vercel-mitigated (Vercel); captcha-delivery.com, the datadome cookie,
x-datadome, x-datadome-cid and x-dd-b (DataDome); the block-page pattern,
_pxAction, _px3, _pxhd, x-px-authorization and _pxAppId (HUMAN/PerimeterX);
_abck, akamai-cache-status, x-akamai-session-info and bmak.sensor_data
(Akamai); x-iinfo, x-cdn: Incapsula, incap_ses_*, visid_incap_*, reese84, the
_Incapsula_Resource pattern and the incapsula/imperva call pattern (Imperva);
x-kasada, x-kasada-challenge, __kasada and kasada.js (Kasada); and the
block-page and verify-page rules for reCAPTCHA, hCaptcha and Turnstile. The
cf-mitigated and x-amzn-waf-action signals come from the vendors'
documentation and also appear in is-antibot.

